     &\Longrightarrow \bb{E}[Y\medspace | \medspace S]=|\bb{E}[Y\medspace | \medspace S]|.
 \end{align}

Using the law of total expectation,     
 \begin{align}\label{eq:total-prob}
     0=\bb{E}[Y]=\bb{E}[\bb{E}[Y\medspace | \medspace S]]=\bb{E}\sqbr{|\bb{E}[Y\medspace | \medspace S]|}.
 \end{align}

From expectation properties, equation~(\ref{eq:total-prob}) yields $\bb{E}[Y|S]=0$, but this is a contradiction to equation~(\ref{eq:random-to-det}).

Thus there is some $s$ for which $\bb{E}[R\medspace | \medspace S=s]\geq\bb{E}[R]$, proving that the deterministic auction $\auc{A}'\coloneq \auc{A}\medspace | \medspace S=s$ has at least as much reward as $\auc{A}$.

